{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548258-ghost-in-vampire","id":1548258,"title":"Ghost in Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-06T09:43:52-08:00","id":1548258,"title":"Ghost in Vampire","content":"Greetings all, need some help, or ideas. I am running a VtM game set in Chicago, early rise of Kevin Jackson, one of my players has a very big interest in ghost etc. She is a Malkavian with 3 Levels in Auspex, Merits- Medium and Spirit Mentor. She has Background in Occult Library. We have had recently a little passage of time; she is wanting to use this time to find or locate ghost in their established domain. <br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I know very little about the WOD ghost and was looking to see if there was some good insight on how to work this. Occult+ Manipulation, research Rituals. I know she can sense them being a Medium, but I would like to flesh this out a bit. Right now, I am considering making a few deceased and giving them some flavor to where she can start learning about them.<br /> <br /> This is also a PbP (play by post) campaign. Guess the jumbled mess above looking for some good ideas where a player who is trying to speak with ghost could go. Help fleshing it out. <br /> <br /> Thanks, as always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T10:31:10-08:00","id":1548261,"title":"","content":"Well, since the WOD has multiple game lines dedicated to ghosts you can go very deep with how much you want to flesh out the ghosts themselves and player interaction with them. For simple interactions, the player's Merits, Disciplines, and Backgrounds would be sufficient for her to find a ghost in Chicago without much trouble.<br /> <br /> Very basic summary of Wraiths from a Vampire perspective:<br /> <br /> - They are attracted to strong emotions<br /> - They can see and hear what is happening like a living person<br /> - They can use 'Disciplines' to affect the living world and go through walls (limited, requires 'juice' like a Bloodpool or Willpower)<br /> - They like to hang out in eerie places where the barrier between the living and dead worlds are thinner and they can interact more easily<br /> - They have objects from the time they were living that are very important to them<br /> - Their 'Beast' is conscious and actively tries to bring out the worst in them<br /> - There is a whole society on the other side they are part of, with its own demands and responsibilities. Officially they are forbidden from interacting with the living.<br /> <br /> For the player to deepen research and familiarity with Wraiths, the go-to would be to learn a Necromancy Path that allows active interaction with the Shadowlands or its inhabitants and explore it that way, although it is entirely possible to do so with just the Medium and Spirit Mentor traits. Note that for the latter, Spirits and Wraiths are different and exist in separate dimensions.<br /> <br /> As for where to find ghosts, cemeteries and haunted places are cliche but actually work. The Shroud (dimensional barrier) between worlds is thinner there, which is why they are haunted in the first place. The other type of place is somewhere where emotions run high, because they feed on them. A sports stadium, a betting parlor, the red light district, a night club. If they need to, they can use their powers to be spooky and enhance or incite emotions - these can be subtle or dramatic, from making someone trip to have the walls bleeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T11:25:21-08:00","id":1548263,"title":"","content":"I second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>'s answer and add: most Necromancy paths are about controlling the dead, not merely being in touch with them. Only the Ash Path would be strictly needed to pop in and out of the Shadowlands if that's what you want the character to do, and you don't want to let him do that in some other way. The Cenotaph Path is also very interesting for characters who wish to interact with ghosts in quirky ways. <br /> <br /> Some Dementation powers are very good at creating situations where ghosts can feed on passions. This can be a tool for the Malkavian to negotiate and develop friendships with ghosts. <br /> I would also say that a character with Medium who invests in his connection to the Shadowlands could justifiably come up with alternative Auspex powers that give access to ghosts. Auspex 2, see them; Auspex 3, sense their fetters and influence on objects; Auspex 4, communicate with them in a way beyond Medium; Auspex 5, step into their world. A Spirit (ghost, rather, unless it's a spirit of death) Mentor could further justify this, or justify learning select powers of Necromancy. Personally, I would prefer the use of Auspex over Necro because Necro - based on how it's written - is based on the vampire corpse being a bridge to the Underworld. That's rather specific and I think it should belong in with specific magical traditions. Auspex, on the other side, is a more general openness to extrasensorial perceptions, and in KotEK it's already suggested it may be used for spirits or ghosts. A vampire with Medium and Spirit Mentor has enough reason, I think, to unlock Auspex in that direction in addition to its normal powers. It's like: Auspex expands your senses, including your empathy and intuition, until you can do weird things with thought and soul (astral projection). Anyone with Medium already has an extra sense, and it makes sense that Auspex would amplify that too if he works on it. <br /> If I recall correctly, some wraiths have a penchant for prophecy, too, so one could link that to the Malk's Eyes of Chaos eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T16:57:37-08:00","id":1548278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justicar-Seth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548258-ghost-in-vampire#post1548258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I know very little about the WOD ghost and was looking to see if there was some good insight on how to work this. Occult+ Manipulation, research Rituals. I know she can sense them being a Medium, but I would like to flesh this out a bit. Right now, I am considering making a few deceased and giving them some flavor to where she can start learning about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>For people who don't have Wraith, my advice is to rely on what you &quot;know&quot; from traditional ghost stories you've read, heard, or watched rather than trying to learn tidbits of Wraith mechanics and lore second hand.<br /> <br /> All you need to do is direct her towards a haunted house. There are always popular stories told about places that are haunted in the real world. The World of Darkness has to have even more. Either create a haunted house (which could be a hotel, restaurant, theatre, cemetary, stretch of country road, whatever, not just a house) on your own, steal one from fiction, or adapt a real one from Chicago folklore.<br /> <br /> Then populate it with one or more ghosts. Since this is something for the PC to interact with, be sure to make the ghost as someone that would be interesting for the player. (And has a reason to WANT to communicate with the PC) Think about how communication between the two begins. The ghost will be able to hear and understand the PC just fine, but may have trouble communicating back. At first the ghost may communicate by odd knocks and sounds that simply confirm to the PC that she has established some kind of communication. Later the ghost may find more tangible means of communication - leaving written messages on fogged up mirrors, playing certain music on their music players, leaving pages open on certain books, strange dreams while the vampire sleeps, and so on. Make it spooky and mysterious because mundane encounters with the ghost would rob of it anything cool. Be sure that the &quot;relationship&quot; between the PC and ghost advances with the PC keep increasing her understanding of the ghost and its desires, but hold off as long as you can before any kind of direct communication between them happens.<br /> <br /> Besides that you will want things like old newspaper clippings telling about how people died, urban legends and campfire tales the locals tell about the ghost, interviewing past inhabitants or visitors of the haunted place, perhaps even getting in contact with others who are better at contacting the dead than they are, and so on.<br /> <br /> If you have more than one ghost, I'd wait to introduce them until the PC establishes a strong relationship with the one ghost who would best be a &quot;partner&quot; for them, and then that NPC ghost can introduce her to the other ghosts in her circle.<br /> <br /> Keep dice rolls to a minimum. Keep advancing the story, but keep having it change based on the PC's actions. Keep things as mysterious and spooky as you can without scaring away the PC or frustrating the player so she abandons it as not fun.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T22:37:11-08:00","id":1548285,"title":"","content":"In VDA20 Tome of Secrets there is a merit, Enchantment (I think that's the name), which can be purchased also after char gen for 6 xp. It includes the option for a ritual to summon a single specific creature, like a particular ghost the PC has a relationship with. The Malk could learn several of these as he connects to more ghosts, so there's an easy way to keep in touch with them even if they're not nearby at the start of the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}